{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The types every other module shares: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event is a value that conforms to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":". Its stored properties"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are its properties, so a misspelled or mistyped one is a compile error. Its type gives the name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destinations record it under, the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" whose consent decides whether it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered, and the version of its shape. Each has a default: the type’s name,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and 1."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two property types carry rules of their own. A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value, such as an email address,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prints as ","type":"text"},{"code":"<redacted>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and has no public accessor: a destination reads it through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord\/reveal(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which gives ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once a delivery has redacted the record. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value satisfies every ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Constraint","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refinement","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" lists, checked once as it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"made: its initializer throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/UnsatisfiedConstraint","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a value that breaks one. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Constraint","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" spelling throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/InvalidConstraint","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for an argument no schema can hold, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a negative length.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A tracker (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trackers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") makes an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of each event it tracks: the event, its own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random identifier, when and where it was tracked, and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it was tracked in.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Destinations receive batches of these records. An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Enricher","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" adds to a record’s context: a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker runs it on every record, or a destination’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"enriched(by:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the records it receives.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare an event with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", part of ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). It derives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" conformance from the struct’s declaration and fills in its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" beside a property fills in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event\/constraintViolation()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". To write the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conformance by hand instead, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import Traffluent","","enum PlanName: Refinement {","    static var constraints: [Constraint<String>] {","        get throws(InvalidConstraint) { try [.minLength(1), .maxLength(32)] }","    }","}","","@Event(consent: .functional)","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: Refined<String, PlanName>","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}","","let event = SignedUp(plan: try Refined(\"pro\"), email: Sensitive(\"ada@example.com\"))","let record = EventRecord(event: event, timestamp: .now, sourceLocation: nil)","let name = record.name  \/\/ \"SignedUp\"","let email = record.reveal(event.email)  \/\/ nil: a record made by hand keeps its sensitive values redacted","let empty = try? Refined<String, PlanName>(\"\")  \/\/ nil: it throws UnsatisfiedConstraint.minLength"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The umbrella guide on this area is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema\/Enumeration","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent"],"anchor":"Events"},{"title":"Property values","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refinement","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Constraint","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ValidationKeyword","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/UnsatisfiedConstraint","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/InvalidConstraint","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConstraintViolation"],"anchor":"Property-values"},{"title":"Records","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SourceLocation","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Enricher"],"anchor":"Records"},{"title":"Context a store keeps","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SessionKey","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SampleRateKey","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SampleRate","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/InvalidSampleRate","doc